{"type":"text","timestamp":1794547640501,"sessionID":"ses_e2ca2abe4ffej8sLiN9Q1dVjE0","part":{"id":"prt_1d35fdceb001unMm7lwssl5vT9","sessionID":"ses_e2ca2abe4ffej8sLiN9Q1dVjE0","messageID":"msg_1d35fd540001vz86K57DUtzf6e","type":"text","text":"T031 done. Comment only, no code changed.\n\n**File written**\n`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` — three comment lines directly above `const offered = landed.some(...)` at line 490:\n\n```js\n      // True when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge,\n      // so this is a reach measure. It is not whether a brief head offered the\n      // command, which the behaviour run line records as `offeredCommand`.\n```\n\nI checked the flag's consumers before writing it: `landed` comes from `recommendationIds`, which slices to the top three, and `offered` feeds `false_offer` and `slashOfferedOnPartial`, so the reach-measure reading is accurate rather than a paraphrase of the task line.\n\n**Verify output** (`CAP` = the capture script; `FLOOR` = `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer'`)\n\n```\ncheck_exit=0\n{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}\n{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}\nfloor_exit=0\n```\n\n`node --check` exits 0, and both floor lines match the expected values exactly.\n\n**Diff check.** `git diff -U0` on the file shows 3 insertions and 0 deletions, all `//` comment lines, confirming no code change. The comment carries no spec path, phase number, task id or requirement id, and uses no em dash or semicolon.\n\n**Not done.** The checkbox at `tasks.md` T031 is unticked, as instructed.\n\nNothing is blocked on you.","time":{"start":1794547637483,"end":1794547640501}}}
